<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yunnan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yunnan is a province of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> bordering Myanmar, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunming">Kunming</a> as its capital. Its plateau was the base of the Nanzhao and Dali kingdoms until the Mongol conquest of 1253, after which it was ruled as a province of China. Home to more ethnic groups than any other Chinese province, it was the scene of the Panthay rebellion of 1856–1873.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yunnan.jpg" alt="Yunnan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:55936-Lijiang_(27941831943).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
